{
	"_comment":	"First-person arms layer (docs/CAMERA_HOLDPOINT.md \"Rule 3\"): the arms + held item drawn with their own camera. Per hold point state (and per item under \"items\"): offset (right, up, forward m), rotation (pitch, yaw, roll deg) and scale (0.9 .. 1.1) about the hold point, fov_add (deg on the Weapon Field of View); in ADS only offset[2] (push), rotation[2] (roll) and scale (about the sight) apply. camera: the arms camera's own position against the eye (right, up, forward m; it moves, never turns), the hip framing (docs/CAMERA_HOLDPOINT.md \"Framing\"); aimed it is back on the eye. equip: the raise from below the view. seam (on: arm vertices near the shoulder blend from the world camera (r0) to the arms camera (r1); off: the arms camera draws only the arms + item). weapon_fov: the Weapon Field of View presets (hip, horizontal deg at 16:9; the layer moves sideways with them so the sight keeps its place on screen). Edit live with arms_tuner.",
